OL,4,G1200FPrivate Passions
OL,5,     GMichael Berkeley's guest is the
OL,6,     Gcameraman and writer James Aldred.
OL,7,G1330FMusic Map
OL,8,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch explores
OL,9,     GWagner's Siegfried Idyll - a
OL,10,     Gpiece written as a birthday
OL,11,     Gpresent for his wife. Featuring
OL,12,     Gmore musical gifts from J.S.
OL,13,     GBach, Bartok and Billie Holiday.
OL,14,G1500FMusic Matters: Music on the Front
OL,15,     FLine
OL,16,     GClive Myrie is in conversation
OL,17,     Gwith fellow journalists. He and
OL,18,     GCaroline share stories to reveal
OL,19,     Gthe power and significance of
OL,20,     Gmusic when reporting from extreme
OL,21,     Gconflict situations.
